# CODEOWNERS — workshop sample
#
# Replace every @your-org/* placeholder with real GitHub teams in your own organization
# before you reuse this file. Placeholder teams do not exist, so GitHub cannot request
# reviews from them. This sample is not a dependable merge gate until real owners and
# repository rules are configured.
# Multiple owners on one pattern route to all listed owners, but a code-owner requirement can
# be satisfied by any one of them. Enforce distinct role approvals separately when required.
# See governance/ownership-raci.md for who these roles map to.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern> <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Later matching lines win, so order from general to specific.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                                   @your-org/prompt-owners

# Workshop delivery content.
/README.md                          @your-org/workshop-maintainers
/facilitator-guide.md               @your-org/workshop-maintainers
/participant-workbook.md            @your-org/workshop-maintainers
/train-the-trainer.md               @your-org/workshop-maintainers
/slides/                            @your-org/workshop-maintainers

# The shared prompt and agent library: the highest-risk content in the repository.
/library/prompts/                   @your-org/prompt-owners
/library/agents/                    @your-org/agent-owners
/library/CHANGELOG.md               @your-org/prompt-owners @your-org/governance-owners

# Contracts that other artifacts depend on. Changes here are breaking changes.
/exercises/03-structured-output.schema.json   @your-org/agent-owners @your-org/governance-owners
/exercises/04-tool-contract.json              @your-org/agent-owners
/exercises/06-test-cases.jsonl                @your-org/prompt-owners @your-org/quality-owners

# Governance rules require governance approval, by definition.
/governance/                        @your-org/governance-owners
/.github/                           @your-org/governance-owners

# Optional paths that depend on product access some people do not have.
/optional/                          @your-org/workshop-maintainers
